    skos:definition "Assay that measures the humoral immune response mediated by the concerted actions of antigen-presenting cells, T lymphocytes, and B lymphocytes, generally by determination of murine primary IgM or IgG antibodies directed against the T-cell-dependent sheep red blood cell (SRBC) surface antigens after in vivo sensitization."@en ;
